\check All Reports
\submenu Phil_new
\script All_Reports.py
\description Runs Report of TOC, Report of Titles, Report of Section Heads, Report of Quotation marks, Report of Poetry errors, Report of Nested Styles, Report of Marker Spaces, Report of Footnotes, Report of Figure Captions, and Report of Capital at Verse, in that order, and combines their individual HTML reports into one AllReportsReport.html (opened automatically). This results list is intentionally just a status message -- run a check individually if you need its itemized list of issues. Any check whose script cannot be found (not yet deployed to this cms folder) is shown as a skipped section instead of stopping the run. The Include options below let you turn off individual checks for a given run; all default to Yes. The remaining options are Capital at Verse's own settings, forwarded through to that check when it runs.
\books
\noText
\toList
\utf8

\optionName IncludeToc
\optionLocalizedName Include Report of TOC
\optionDescription Set to No to skip the TOC check for this run.
\optionDefault Yes

\optionName IncludeTitles
\optionLocalizedName Include Report of Titles
\optionDescription Set to No to skip the Titles check for this run.
\optionDefault Yes

\optionName IncludeSectionHeads
\optionLocalizedName Include Report of Section Heads
\optionDescription Set to No to skip the Section Heads check for this run.
\optionDefault Yes

\optionName IncludeQuotationMarks
\optionLocalizedName Include Report of Quotation marks
\optionDescription Set to No to skip the Quotation marks check for this run.
\optionDefault Yes

\optionName IncludePoetryErrors
\optionLocalizedName Include Report of Poetry errors
\optionDescription Set to No to skip the Poetry errors check for this run.
\optionDefault Yes

\optionName IncludeNestedStyles
\optionLocalizedName Include Report of Nested Styles
\optionDescription Set to No to skip the Nested Styles check for this run.
\optionDefault Yes

\optionName IncludeMarkerSpaces
\optionLocalizedName Include Report of Marker Spaces
\optionDescription Set to No to skip the Marker Spaces check for this run.
\optionDefault Yes

\optionName IncludeFootnotes
\optionLocalizedName Include Report of Footnotes
\optionDescription Set to No to skip the Footnotes check for this run.
\optionDefault Yes

\optionName IncludeFigureCaptions
\optionLocalizedName Include Report of Figure Captions
\optionDescription Set to No to skip the Figure Captions check for this run.
\optionDefault Yes

\optionName IncludeCapitalAtVerse
\optionLocalizedName Include Report of Capital at Verse
\optionDescription Set to No to skip the Capital at Verse check for this run.
\optionDefault Yes

\optionName FinalPunctuation
\optionLocalizedName Sentence-final characters
\optionDescription Forwarded to Report of Capital at Verse. Characters that END a sentence. Verses following any of these are not flagged. Extend with language-specific closing quotes if needed.
\optionDefault .!?

\optionName WordsToIgnore
\optionLocalizedName Words to ignore
\optionDescription Forwarded to Report of Capital at Verse. Comma-separated list of capitalized words that should not be flagged (e.g. Senor, Alfa, Espiritu). Use this for proper nouns not covered by TermRenderings.xml. This is also the base-word list that Word prefixes/suffixes to ignore build on: a listed word with one of those prefixes or suffixes attached is also not flagged.
\optionDefault

\optionName IgnoreBiblicalTerms
\optionLocalizedName Ignore capitalized Biblical Terms
\optionDescription Forwarded to Report of Capital at Verse. Set to Yes to skip a capitalized word or phrase that is a rendering in the project's Biblical Terms (TermRenderings.xml), such as a proper name. Set to No to flag these too.
\optionDefault Yes

\optionName IgnoreWordlistCapitals
\optionLocalizedName Ignore capitalized words in the Wordlist
\optionDescription Forwarded to Report of Capital at Verse. Set to Yes to skip a word that the project's Wordlist marks as always capitalized (a specific case in SpellingStatus.xml).
\optionDefault Yes

\optionName IgnoreCapAfterQuote
\optionLocalizedName Ignore capital after opening quote
\optionDescription Forwarded to Report of Capital at Verse. Set to Yes to suppress errors where a verse begins with a capitalized word immediately after an opening quotation mark (e.g. direct speech). The characters treated as openers are configured by the Opening quote characters option below.
\optionDefault No

\optionName QuoteOpeningChars
\optionLocalizedName Opening quote characters
\optionDescription Forwarded to Report of Capital at Verse. Characters treated as opening quotation marks when "Ignore capital after opening quote" is set to Yes. Each character in this string is an opener. Default covers left guillemet («), left double curly quote (“), em dash (—), and left single curly quote (‘). Clear this field to fall back to Unicode Pi-category detection.
\optionDefault «“—‘

\optionName IgnoreStyles
\optionLocalizedName Character styles to ignore
\optionDescription Forwarded to Report of Capital at Verse. Comma-separated USFM character style names (no backslash) whose enclosed text is excluded when detecting the last character of a verse. Use for styles like qs (Selah) or pn (proper names) that do not end with sentence-final punctuation.
\optionDefault

\optionName IgnoreParaStyles
\optionLocalizedName Paragraph styles to ignore
\optionDescription Forwarded to Report of Capital at Verse. Comma-separated USFM paragraph marker names (no backslash) whose text is excluded when computing the last character of a verse. Default covers: sp (speaker), r (parallel reference), ms/mr (major section), sr (section range). Section headings (s, s1, s2...) are suppressed automatically without this option. A paragraph break whose only text before the next verse is from these styles (e.g. \s1 heading, then \sp speaker, then \q1) also suppresses the check.
\optionDefault sp, r, ms, mr, sr

\optionName PrefixesToIgnore
\optionLocalizedName Word prefixes to ignore
\optionDescription Forwarded to Report of Capital at Verse. Space-separated list of word prefixes (e.g. ra Ra). A capitalized verse-start word made of one of these plus either a word listed in Words to ignore, or a capitalized Biblical Terms rendering this check already recognizes from TermRenderings.xml (case-insensitive), will not be flagged. An entry can also be a "/"-separated group of interchangeable variants (e.g. i/ɨ/ʉ) for languages where attaching the prefix changes the following letter(s).
\optionDefault

\optionName SuffixesToIgnore
\optionLocalizedName Word suffixes to ignore
\optionDescription Forwarded to Report of Capital at Verse. Space-separated list of word suffixes (e.g. es am). A capitalized verse-start word made of one of these plus either a word listed in Words to ignore, or a capitalized Biblical Terms rendering this check already recognizes from TermRenderings.xml (case-insensitive), will not be flagged. An entry can also be a "/"-separated group of interchangeable variants (e.g. ion/iones, or ɨ/ʉ) for languages where the stem's ending changes when a suffix attaches.
\optionDefault

\optionName MidWordPunctuation
\optionLocalizedName Mid-word punctuation
\optionDescription Forwarded to Report of Capital at Verse. Characters that may appear inside a word (e.g. - for hyphen, ' for apostrophe). Enter without spaces. Words containing these characters are treated as a single unit when checking for capitals.
\optionDefault -

\optionName SkipBeforeVerse
\optionLocalizedName Characters to skip before a verse number
\optionDescription Forwarded to Report of Capital at Verse. Characters (no spaces) that may stand just before a verse number, such as the [ that opens a bracketed verse. They are looked past when finding how the previous verse ended, so "word. [" counts as ending with . and a paragraph marker followed only by [ counts as a paragraph break. Clear this field to treat them as ordinary characters.
\optionDefault [
